!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-sibling-declared-after-its-dependent-field-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2"
  description: """
    A record's fields are a telescope: a field may depend only on fields declared before it, in the order of `fields`.
    `kind` comes after `v`, so `kind!` is refused at the declaration. That is also why no cycle check is needed: in `{
    a: b! b: a! }` one of the two refers to a later field.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
